  ('3dd35700-943e-5264-ad06-a44982ca9cc3', 30, 'Day 30 — coming soon', '', '', '[]'::jsonb, 'What did you do today, and what did you notice?', 0, false),
  ('3dd35700-943e-5264-ad06-a44982ca9cc3', 31, 'Day 31 — coming soon', '', '', '[]'::jsonb, 'What did you do today, and what did you notice?', 0, false),
  ('33721a9a-e30c-5b65-aa47-b904fe2bfd83', 1, 'Choose the person, not the goal', 'Lasting change comes from deciding who you want to be, then proving it to yourself with small wins. Every action is a vote for a type of person. You don''t need a perfect record — you need a majority of votes.', 'Atomic Habits — James Clear', '["Finish this sentence: ''I am the kind of person who…''","Pick ONE habit that person would do every day.","Make it small enough to do in two minutes.","Do it once today, right after you finish this task."]'::jsonb, 'Who are you becoming, and what is the two-minute habit you chose?', 0, true),
  ('33721a9a-e30c-5b65-aa47-b904fe2bfd83', 2, 'Find your cue', 'Every habit runs on a loop: a cue, a routine and a reward. Habits don''t stick because we want them to — they stick when something in the day reliably triggers them. Tie a new routine to a cue that already happens every day.', 'The Power of Habit — Charles Duhigg', '["List three things you already do every single day (coffee, brushing teeth, opening your laptop).","Pick one as your cue.","Write your plan: ''After I [cue], I will [habit].''","Run it once today."]'::jsonb, 'What is your ''After I…, I will…'' sentence, and did you run it today?', 0, true),
  ('33721a9a-e30c-5b65-aa47-b904fe2bfd83', 3, 'Do it when you don''t feel like it', 'Most of us stop long before we are actually done — the mind asks to quit well before the body has to. Discipline grows in the moments you''d rather not, because those are the only moments that train it. Small voluntary discomfort makes the big ones easier.', 'Can''t Hurt Me — David Goggins', '["Pick the moment today when you least want to do your habit.","Do it then, on purpose.","Notice the excuse your mind offers. Write it down word for word."]'::jsonb, 'What excuse did your mind give you today, and what did you do anyway?', 0, true),
  ('33721a9a-e30c-5b65-aa47-b904fe2bfd83', 4, 'Day 4 — coming soon', '', '', '[]'::jsonb, 'What did you do today, and what did you notice?', 0, false),
