  ('b9e48da4-691f-5012-ad0c-6f435d1e7990', 1, 'Invite AI to one real task', 'The fastest way to learn what AI can do is to bring it into the work you already do, instead of testing it on toy questions. You are the expert in your own tasks, so you can judge its answers better than anyone. Expect it to be surprisingly good at some things and surprisingly bad at others.', 'Co-Intelligence — Ethan Mollick', '["Pick one real thing on your to-do list today: an email, a plan, a decision.","Open any AI chat tool and ask for help with exactly that.","Give it context: who it''s for, what you want, what good looks like.","Use, edit or throw away the result — your call."]'::jsonb, 'What task did you bring to AI, and was the result better or worse than you expected?', 0, true),
  ('b9e48da4-691f-5012-ad0c-6f435d1e7990', 2, 'Give it a role', 'AI answers improve when you tell it who to be and who it is talking to. Treating it like a capable colleague — with a role, a goal and constraints — works better than typing a search query. The more specific the person, the more useful the answer.', 'Co-Intelligence — Ethan Mollick', '["Take a question you''d normally search for.","Ask it plainly first and save the answer.","Ask again, starting with: ''You are a [specific expert]. I am a [who you are]. Help me…''","Compare the two answers."]'::jsonb, 'What role did you give the AI, and how did the second answer differ from the first?', 0, true),
  ('b9e48da4-691f-5012-ad0c-6f435d1e7990', 3, 'Catch it being wrong', 'AI can sound completely confident while being incorrect, so the human has to stay in the loop. Your job is not to accept or reject AI — it''s to check it where it matters. Knowing how it fails is what makes it safe to use.', 'Co-Intelligence — Ethan Mollick', '["Ask AI about something you know very well: your job, your city, your hobby.","Read the answer carefully and look for one thing that is wrong or made up.","Tell the AI what it got wrong and see how it responds."]'::jsonb, 'What did the AI get wrong, and how will that change the way you use it?', 0, true),
  ('b9e48da4-691f-5012-ad0c-6f435d1e7990', 4, 'Day 4 — coming soon', '', '', '[]'::jsonb, 'What did you do today, and what did you notice?', 0, false),
