  ('b9e48da4-691f-5012-ad0c-6f435d1e7990', 21, 'Day 21 — coming soon', '', '', '[]'::jsonb, 'What did you do today, and what did you notice?', 0, false),
  ('ee91d74f-807f-5be5-a70a-95e266c4bbc9', 1, 'Take a 10-minute walk', 'Staying able to move well for decades matters more than any short burst of fitness, and regular easy movement is the base that makes it possible. The best exercise is the one you''ll still be doing next year. Starting small is not a compromise — it''s the strategy.', 'Outlive — Peter Attia', '["Not medical advice — check with a doctor before starting new exercise.","Walk for 10 minutes today at a comfortable pace. Outside if you can.","Leave your headphones off for the first two minutes and just notice how you feel.","Pick the time you''ll walk tomorrow."]'::jsonb, 'When did you walk, how did you feel afterwards, and what time will you walk tomorrow?', 0, true),
  ('ee91d74f-807f-5be5-a70a-95e266c4bbc9', 2, 'Set a fixed wake-up time', 'Sleep works best on a regular rhythm. Waking at the same time every day — weekends included — anchors your body clock more than almost anything else you can do. Consistency matters more than any single long night.', 'Why We Sleep — Matthew Walker', '["Choose one wake-up time you can keep all seven days.","Set a repeating alarm for it now.","Count back 8 hours: that is your target time to be in bed.","Take today''s 10-minute walk."]'::jsonb, 'What wake-up time did you choose, and what will you change tonight to make it easier?', 0, true),
  ('ee91d74f-807f-5be5-a70a-95e266c4bbc9', 3, 'Attach your walk to something you already do', 'New habits stick best when they are stacked onto ones you already have. Instead of relying on motivation, give the habit a fixed place in your day. The clearer the trigger, the less you have to decide.', 'Atomic Habits — James Clear', '["Pick a daily anchor: after lunch, after work, after dinner.","Say it out loud: ''After I [anchor], I walk for 10 minutes.''","Put your shoes where you will see them at that time.","Do today''s walk at that moment."]'::jsonb, 'What is your anchor, and did the walk feel easier when it had a fixed place in your day?', 0, true),
